   "desc": "No internet price tags — honest national ASPS average surgeon-fee data for 20 procedures, what moves the number, and financing in plain terms.",
   "faqs": [
    {
     "a": "Because a real quote requires an examination. A published number would either be a teaser (dishonest) or a ceiling (wrong for complex cases). What we will do: show you the national data above, examine you, and hand you one written, all-in number that we honor.",
     "q": "Why won’t you just publish your prices?"
    },
    {
     "a": "Consultation policies are confirmed when you book — call 405-751-0042. The wellness program currently advertises a $99 peptide-consultation special on its own page; surgical consult policy is quoted when you schedule.",
     "q": "Is the consultation itself free?"
    },
    {
     "a": "Cosmetic procedures are self-pay. A narrow exception in the national data: breast reduction is “often covered by health insurance plans” when medically indicated (ASPS) — candidacy and coverage are determined case-by-case.",
     "q": "Does insurance ever apply?"
    },
    {
     "a": "That’s exactly what financing consults are for — and why we publish the monthly-payment framing beside the ranges. Bring your target number; the team will tell you honestly what’s achievable.",
     "q": "What if the national average is above my budget?"
    }
   ],
